  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-16T14:27:33.940Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've authored many worlds with custom shaders, and I'm interested in updating them with SPS-I support so that they don't become obsolete, but I'm not sure how to confirm that I've done so correctly. Could there be a debug option that would temporarily force disabling support for non-SPS-I shaders, to verify that worlds are set up correctly for the eventual deprecation?",
